<ontology/use_rubber_waterproofing/use_rubber_waterproofing__0015__q1/#resource> dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. GAS-LIGHT" ;
    dcterms:source <https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/44562> ;
    a <ontology/EvidenceQuote/#resource> ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Caoutchouc used in India-Rubber, Gutta-Percha & Waterproofing: Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. GAS-LIGHT"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "The coal oil when rectified by distillation, is extensively employed for dissolving caoutchouc in making the varnish of waterproof cloth, and also for burning in a peculiar kind of lamps under the name of naphtha."@en ;
    <ontology/retrievalMode/#resource> "direct_sentence" .
